  "vendor_website": "masibus.com",
  "revision": 3,
  "source": "Masibus PM2160-A User's Manual, doc. ref. m20Aom201, issue 02",
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU on RS-485, 9600/19200/38400 baud (selectable), 1 start bit, 1 stop bit; slave address 1-247 set on the meter. Function 04 reads the measurements, 03 reads and 06 writes the configuration. Master time-out: 4 s or more.",
    "Addresses are the manual's 3xxxx/4xxxx references minus 30001/40001, i.e. wire addresses starting at 0. Measurements are two registers each; read an even number of registers.",
    "Data type is selected by configuration register 40121: 1 = Long (integer, multiply by the factor in the \"scale\" column), 0 = Real (IEEE float, the value is then already in the shown unit). This map describes the Long format. The manual says to use \"swapped long\" / \"swapped float\" in the master, taken here as the low word first. Real mode uses the same addresses.",
    "Energy and demand are in kilo units after the factor (kWh, kvarh, kVAh). Signedness of the Long values is not stated: unsigned is assumed.",
    "Registers marked Reserved in the manual are left out.",
    "The compact block at 32001 repeats the main totals in one contiguous read. The manual leaves the names of 32029 and 32031 blank: they are taken to be total Varh import and export, following the order of the main table.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
